{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.MotivicSubstrate"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.frobenius_realize_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.frobenius_realize_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-galois-character.lean#L96-L96","doc":"**Realization-tower compatibility.**\n\nAt every finite place whose realization target is nontrivial, the\nlocal Frobenius character is *visible in the tower*: its image\nunder the substrate's realization map at that place is nonzero.\n\nWithout it the class carries a single data field and no Prop field\nat all, so `⟨fun _ => 0⟩` inhabits it and every downstream\n`[MotivicGaloisCharacter …]` hypothesis is discharged by a character\nthat is identically zero.\n\n**Scope.**  The full compatibility of `χ^mot_{A,p}` with the\nrealization tower would relate `frobenius_at p` to a Frobenius\n*operator* on `Target (Place.finite p)`.  `MotivicSubstrate` supplies\nno such operator, so that statement is not expressible here.  What is\nencoded is the non-degeneracy half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.frobenius_at","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.frobenius_at","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-galois-character.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Local Frobenius eigenvalue at a finite prime `p`,\nrepresented as an element of the dimension-completion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter.mk","kind":"ctor","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-galois-character.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicGaloisCharacter","kind":"class","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-galois-character.lean#L56-L98","doc":"**Motivic Galois character of a Frobenius–Hopf substrate.**\n\nAxiomatic class encoding the cyclotomic-Galois action on the\nmotivic class `[A]` of the substrate.  Parameters:\n* `K0 Mhat` — Grothendieck ring + dimension-completion\n  ([`MotivicSubstrate`](MotivicSubstrate)).\n* `Target` — realisation target functor (passed through to\n  `MotivicSubstrate`).\n* `motiveA : Mhat` — the motivic class of the substrate $A$.\n\nThe class **takes a `MotivicSubstrate` instance as a\nhypothesis** (per `def:motivic-galois-character` narrative),\nmaking the Galois character genuinely local to a substrate\nrather than free-floating type parameters.\n\nRef: [yekutieli2010], [tate1967]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:motivic-galois-character","label":"def:motivic-galois-character","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/motivic-galois-character.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}